{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve this problem, we need to determine the volume of the ice sphere and compare it to the volume of the cone to find out how much water will overflow when the ice melts.\n\n1. **Calculate the volume of the ice sphere:**\n   The formula for the volume of a sphere is given by:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{sphere}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3\n   \\]\n   Here, the radius \\( r \\) of the sphere is 4. So, we substitute \\( r = 4 \\) into the formula:\n   \\[\n   V_{\\text{sphere}} = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (4)^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\cdot 64 = \\frac{256}{3} \\pi\n   \\]\n\n","prefix_end":534,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,419,3491,11,582,1184,311,8253,279,8123,315,279,9853,25366,323,9429,432,311,279,8123,315,279,22161,311,1477,700,1246,1753,3015,686,16484,979,279,9853,98091,382,16,13,3070,47866,279,8123,315,279,9853,25366,25,1019,256,576,14806,369,279,8123,315,264,25366,374,2661,553,510,256,1124,9640,256,647,15159,59,1318,84386,8023,3417,284,1124,37018,90,19,15170,18,92,1124,2493,435,61,18,198,256,1124,921,256,5692,11,279,10578,17767,435,1124,8,315,279,25366,374,220,19,13,2055,11,582,27679,17767,435,284,220,19,1124,8,1119,279,14806,510,256,1124,9640,256,647,15159,59,1318,84386,8023,3417,284,1124,37018,90,19,15170,18,92,1124,2493,320,19,29776,18,284,1124,37018,90,19,15170,18,92,1124,2493,1124,50853,220,21,19,284,1124,37018,90,17,20,21,15170,18,92,1124,2493,198,256,1124,2533,17,13,3070,47866,279,8123,315,279,22161,25,1019,256,576,14806,369,279,8123,315,264,22161,374,2661,553,510,256,1124,9640,256,647,15159,59,1318,90,58082,3417,284,1124,37018,90,16,15170,18,92,1124,2493,435,61,17,305,198,256,1124,921,256,5692,11,279,10578,17767,435,1124,8,315,279,22161,374,220,19,323,279,2608,17767,305,1124,8,374,220,20,13,2055,11,582,27679,17767,435,284,220,19,1124,8,323,17767,305,284,220,20,1124,8,1119,279,14806,510,256,1124,964